      "message": "I find this solution a lot more complex than is necessary. I especially dislike the necessity for callers to know whether to clear the satisfier, as this means relying on lingering members on objects that are on their way to garbage collection, which I find extremely dangerous.\n\nCounter-proposal ❶ : how about calling incrementCountOrThrow in handleRegisterNetworkRequests immediately after put() instead of in the constructors ? I don\u0027t think any other change would be necessary. The default request would not be counted, which is almost better (or we could count it, it wouldn\u0027t matter). If I\u0027m not mistaken this would be a +1-3 lines change, instead of this +130-25 change.\n\nCounter-proposal ❷ : exempt the system server from the 100 callbacks limit. We\u0027ve been thinking about this for a while anyway. The drawback is that we won\u0027t realize if the system server leaks requests.\n\nI would favor ❶. It sounds simpler and in fact more correct than increasing the count in the constructor for NetworkRequestInfo and doesn\u0027t have the drawback of ❷.",
